  "learnGoalTitle": "The goal",
  "learnGoalBody": "Build a hand of 14 tiles made of four sets plus one pair. Each turn you draw a tile and discard one, working toward that shape. The first player to complete it wins the hand.",
  "learnTilesTitle": "The tiles",
  "learnTilesBody": "There are three suits numbered 1 to 9 (characters, dots and bamboo), plus four winds and three dragons. Some rulesets, Hong Kong among them, add flower tiles: they score a bonus and are replaced from the wall.",
  "learnSetsTitle": "Sets and calls",
  "learnSetsBody": "A set is a run of three in one suit (a chow), three identical tiles (a pong), or four identical tiles (a kong). You can claim another player's discard to finish a set, and a chow only from the player on your left. A claimed set is shown face up.",
  "learnWinTitle": "Winning",
  "learnWinBodyHongKong": "Complete four sets and a pair, by drawing the last tile yourself or claiming a discard, and you win. With the default minimum of 0 faan, any complete hand wins, even the simplest. The guide at the table shows how far you are from a win.",
  "learnWinBodyOther": "Complete four sets and a pair to win, as long as the hand also meets {rules}'s own requirements. The guide at the table shows how far you are from a win.",
