  "glossaryTitle": "Glossary",
  "glossarySearchHint": "Search terms",
  "glossaryNoMatch": "No terms match your search.",
  "glossaryUnitHan": "Han",
  "glossaryUnitFaan": "Faan",
  "glossaryUnitTai": "Tai",
  "glossaryUnitFan": "Fan",
  "glossaryTermSet": "Set",
  "glossaryDefSet": "Three tiles that go together: a run of three in one suit, or three identical tiles. Four identical tiles also count, as a kong.",
  "glossaryTermPair": "Pair",
  "glossaryDefPair": "Two identical tiles. A winning hand is four sets and exactly one pair.",
  "glossaryDefChi": "Claim another player's discard to finish a run of three in one suit. Only from the player on your left; the set is then shown face up.",
  "glossaryDefPon": "Claim a discard that matches two tiles in your hand, from any player, to make three of a kind. The set is shown face up.",
  "glossaryDefKan": "Four identical tiles. You then draw a replacement tile from the end of the wall.",
  "glossaryTermDiscard": "Discard",
  "glossaryDefDiscard": "The tile you throw away at the end of your turn, face up in front of you. Other players may be able to claim it.",
  "glossaryDefTsumo": "Winning on a tile you drew yourself.",
  "glossaryDefRon": "Winning on a tile another player discarded.",
  "glossaryTermDealer": "Dealer",
  "glossaryDefDealer": "The player seated East, who plays first. Winning usually lets the dealer keep the seat for another hand.",
  "glossaryTermWinds": "Winds",
  "glossaryDefWinds": "Four tiles: East, South, West and North. They also name the seats and the round, and a set of your own seat wind or the round wind can be worth extra.",
  "glossaryTermDragons": "Dragons",
  "glossaryDefDragons": "Three tiles: White, Green and Red. A set of any dragon is worth extra.",
  "glossaryTermFlowers": "Flowers",
  "glossaryDefFlowers": "Bonus tiles. When you draw one, you show it and take a replacement from the wall. Each one can add to a winning hand's score.",
  "glossaryTermVoid": "Void suit",
  "glossaryDefVoid": "You give up one of the three suits at the start. While you hold any tile of it, you must discard those first.",
  "glossaryDefScore": "What a winning hand earns. More means a more valuable hand. Some tables set a minimum a hand must reach before it can win.",
  "glossaryTermRiichi": "Riichi",
  "glossaryDefRiichi": "Declare a closed hand one tile from winning by betting 1,000 points. Your hand is then locked: you can only discard each tile you draw. It earns extra score.",
  "glossaryTermDora": "Dora",
  "glossaryDefDora": "Bonus tiles chosen by an indicator tile on the table. Each one in a winning hand adds a han.",
  "glossaryTermFuriten": "Furiten",
  "glossaryDefFuriten": "You can't win off a discard if a tile that would complete your hand is among your own discards. A self-draw still wins.",
  "glossaryTermReady": "Ready hand",
  "glossaryDefReady": "A hand one tile from winning. The guide shows which tiles would finish it.",
  "glossaryTermAway": "Tiles away",
  "glossaryDefAway": "How many more tiles your hand needs before it can win. One tile away means ready. The guide's meter and its Away or Shanten column show it.",
  "glossaryTermHelpful": "Helpful tiles",
  "glossaryDefHelpful": "Tiles you could draw that move your hand closer to winning. The guide counts how many are still unseen.",
